node_modules
dist
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.local
server/data
# Same reasoning as server/data and .env, applied to their backup copy: these
# archives hold password hashes and session tokens. Multi-stage keeps them out
# of the final image, but not out of the build context or the builder layer —
# and a build cache can be exported or pushed.
backups
# The Remotion render worker is a separate sub-project with its own Dockerfile
# and its own build context (worker/video/). Mocky's image copies the tree with
# `COPY . .`, so without this line the default image would carry Remotion source
# — the one thing that is supposed to stay out of it, since keeping Remotion
# away from anyone who has not opted in is the whole point of the separation.
worker
docker-compose.override.yml
.claude
*.md
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
.opencode